<description>&lt;p&gt;Colombia rejected a U.S. proposal for joint anti-drug strikes while President Petro was accused of freezing purchases of equipment to counter armed-group drones. A Trump-backed right-wing lawyer appears to have won the presidential election, and the government secured the release of two ELN hostages through a deal with Venezuela. U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth arrived in Bogotá to reinforce the security agenda. In Kyiv, a 19‑year-old woman was detained for poisoning a Colombian veteran of the Ukrainian Armed Forces for $1,000. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxQSExMVUVnMTI2a2JxR0tCUVMydGRVbDd6dy03bERjVURwc2xVREZuSEh2d3JUQWh6bUN4Q1JXTHB1YThoRHdXZU83N1RscDl1d2ZrdE5lSy1wbjgyMTNYV1NicDk0MEVyU01jUVpZR21LZkJUZ2ZEbWRYRnRlOEpENFRWMDdZUy1oY1VRT1JrWWhDQ2xIbkJrYnJCNk9hQjRBd0ZHZjZ0b3IyS1lRb205dg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Colombia Reports&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTFA0QTgzNkFGbEVNVTUzWGVaZFJMdHJBZmVSWUE3eG5YcDRYM3lvQ2V2blk1UEpWVnZxTjR5aEpyZU9qNWFsQmRKRzdqcFpYZjdkbWFfRXhfVWQ5WWtuM0UtYWlFWmJMazFlWFY1Mk5XT0YtbFBrYmphZEdCcm1OdWs?oc=5&quot;&gt;Foreign Affairs&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ABC News - Breaking News, Latest News and Videos&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;La Via Campesina&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxOSDhVZml0R2V4TnZJanBHMWg0aUg2cXlNZlFxaFg0VFBqbHZvaWpEUDJtaEFrSER5SzRoS18yb2IyVENSaE9iS3JNVTg1N0ttQ0l3YWVDVllpZGM3WFZBV1VoQzNRMktGcHp5b3NJcFpPRGxnRUFZT3ctZ0hsb3BDdzZOODJIQTY4cWdqNEUtOWdTeDc4UV9fYWRNaUl0U3dFZWp3Wk1ROA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Idaho State Journal&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Ukrinform&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;ht